    {
      "coptic": "ⲟⲩⲟϩ ⲛⲁⲩ**ⲥⲱⲃⲓ** ⲙⲙⲟϥ ⲛⲑⲟϥ ⲇⲉ ⲉⲧⲁϥϩⲓ ⲡⲧⲏⲣϥ ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ⲁϥⲱⲗⲓ ⲛⲉⲙⲁϥ ⲙⲫⲓⲱⲧ ⲛϯⲁⲗⲟⲩ ⲛⲉⲙⲧⲉⲥⲙⲁⲩ ⲛⲉⲙⲛⲏ ⲉⲑⲛⲉⲙⲁϥ ⲟⲩⲟϩ ⲁϥϣⲉ ⲛⲁϥ ⲉϧⲟⲩⲛ ⲉⲡⲓⲙⲁ ⲉⲛⲁⲣⲉϯⲁⲗⲟⲩ ⲭⲏ ⲙⲙⲟϥ .",
      "english": "They ridiculed him. But he, having put them all out, took the father of the child, her mother, and those who were with him, and went in where the child was lying.",
      "source": "Bohairic Gospel of Mark 5 (Digital Edition)",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:nt.mark.bohairic_ed:5",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ϫⲉⲕⲁⲕⲏⲕⲉⲫⲁⲗⲏ · ⲉⲕ**ⲥⲱⲃⲉ** ⲙⲙⲟⲓ ·",
      "english": "O bad head! Wouldst thou make a mock of me?",
      "source": "Martyrdom of Victor part 4",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:martyrdoms.victor.budge:23-32",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲕⲁⲛ ⲁⲕϣⲁⲛϫⲟⲥ ϫⲉⲥⲉⲛⲁⲉⲣⲃⲗⲁⲡⲧⲓⲛ ⲙⲙⲟⲓ ⲁⲛ ⲉⲑⲃⲉⲡⲓⲥⲙⲟⲧ ⲛⲧⲉⲧⲉⲕⲙⲉⲧⲉⲩⲥⲉⲃⲏⲥ ϫⲉⲥⲉⲛⲁϣⲃⲱⲗ ⲙⲡⲉⲧϭⲱⲗⲕ ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ⲁⲛ ⲓⲉ ⲁⲣⲏⲟⲩ ⲭⲛⲁϭⲁⲥⲕ ⲉϫⲱⲟⲩ ⲓⲉ ⲛⲧⲉⲕ**ⲥⲱⲃⲓ** ⲙⲙⲱⲟⲩ",
      "english": "Even if you say, “They will not harm me,” because of the strength of your piety, do not let them weaken your fervor, nor make yourself proud before them, nor mock them.",
      "source": "Bohairic Lausiac History - Part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lausiac.boh_lausiac.amelineau_ed:0",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲡⲉⲛⲧⲁϥⲧⲁⲁⲥ ⲛⲁϥ ⲙⲙⲓⲛⲙⲙⲟϥ ⲉ**ⲥⲱⲃⲉ** ⲛⲛⲉϥϫⲁϫⲉ ·",
      "english": "Who dost Thyself make it to laugh to scorn its enemy.",
      "source": "Dormition of John MERC.AD in Budge ed.",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:misc.dormition_john.budge",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
